@startuml WF-05_Robot_Monitoring_Incident_Handling
title WF-05: Robot Monitoring & Incident Handling (Features F-05, F-06 | Scenarios DS-09, DS-10)\nProject: Intelligent Hotel Concierge Robot (HC-Robot) - FA26SE905 | Baseline: review-2

skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #D97706
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #3B82F6
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontSize 13
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #64748B

|Robot|
start
repeat
  :Publish periodic telemetry stream (2 Hz)\n(Cartesian pose [x, y, yaw], velocity, battery_level,\nLiDAR scan & COM health, ultrasonic sensor status);
  note right
    **Normal Operating State (DS-09)**
    Robot.status = **IDLE** or **NAVIGATING**
  end note

  |Backend|
  :Receive telemetry payload, update fleet status,\nand stream live data over WebSocket;

  |Operations Staff|
  :Monitor live robot position on 2D floor map,\nLiDAR point cloud, and hardware health indicators;

  |Backend|
  :Evaluate hardware/sensor health and multi-tier battery thresholds;

  if (Hardware or battery condition?) then (Normal [DS-09]: Sensors healthy AND Battery > 20%)
    :Maintain normal telemetry monitoring status;

  elseif (Branch A [DS-10]: LiDAR / safety-critical sensor failure?) then (Sensor failure or LiDAR timeout > 1.0s)
    |Robot|
    :Detect LiDAR disconnection or safety sensor fault\nand trigger navigation safety override;
    :Command immediate zero velocity (PWM = 0)\nand halt all unsafe movement;
    note right
      **Branch A State Transition (Sensor Failure)**
      BM01 / ROS2 Node: Robot.status: **IDLE / NAVIGATING -> EMERGENCY_STOP**
      (Backend model comment lists `'ERROR'` alongside ROS2 `'EMERGENCY_STOP'`)
    end note

    |Backend|
    fork
      :Record hardware fault in incident log;
      note right
        **Entity State Transition**
        BM01 Intended: IncidentLog.status = **LOGGED**
        (DB Implementation: LogEvent(category="ROBOT",
        level="CRITICAL") & Notification(type="Warning"))
      end note
    fork again
      :Broadcast emergency alert banner and audio alarm\nto Operations & Maintenance dashboards;
    end fork

    |Operations Staff|
    :Receive sensor failure alert and dispatch Maintenance;

    |Maintenance|
    :Inspect LiDAR / sensor hardware, restore serial/USB link,\nand run safety verification checks;

    |Robot|
    :Verify healthy sensor stream and clear emergency lock;
    note right
      **Recovery State Transition**
      Robot.status: **EMERGENCY_STOP -> IDLE**
    end note

    |Backend|
    :Update incident record and log recovery history;
    note right
      **Entity State Transition**
      BM01 Intended: IncidentLog.status: **LOGGED -> RESOLVED**
    end note

  else (Branch B [DS-10]: Low or Critical Battery [Battery <= 20%])
    |Robot|
    if (Battery level threshold?) then (Warning Buffer: 10% < Battery <= 20% [BATTERY_MODE.LOW])
      :Display low-battery warning banner on screen\nand block new guest sessions;
      if (Currently serving an active guest session?) then (Yes - Serving guest)
        :Allow safe completion of current guest interaction;
      else (No - Idle)
      endif
      :Initiate scheduled return-to-charger navigation\n(Move to CHARGER_STATION);

    else (Critical Cut-off: Battery <= 10% [BATTERY_MODE.CRITICAL])
      :Immediately abort active guest session or navigation task;
      :Play voice apology, display critical battery warning,\nand initiate emergency docking to CHARGER_STATION;
    endif

    :Arrive at CHARGER_STATION, lock guest interaction,\nand enter charging state;
    note right
      **Branch B State Transition (Battery Policy)**
      Robot.status: **IDLE / NAVIGATING -> CHARGING**
      (batteryPolicy.js: waitingForCharge = True)
    end note

    |Backend|
    fork
      :Log low-battery incident and create charging ticket\n(service_type = "ROBOT_CHARGING");
      note right
        **Entity State Transition**
        BM01 Intended: IncidentLog.status = **LOGGED**
        (DB Implementation: SupportRequest.status = **"Pending"**
        assigned to Maintenance + LogEvent)
      end note
    fork again
      :Send high-urgency charging alert to Maintenance\nand Operations Staff;
    end fork

    |Maintenance|
    :Receive charging alert, connect power supply at dock,\nand confirm charging initiation;

    |Robot|
    repeat
      :Monitor battery charge percentage while docked;
    repeat while (Battery >= 80% recovery threshold?) is (No - Battery < 80% [Continue charging]) not (Yes - Battery >= 80% [BATTERY_RESUME_PERCENT])

    |Maintenance|
    :Disconnect charger, perform post-charge checks,\nand authorize operational resumption;

    |Robot|
    :Clear charging lock and resume lobby standby operation;
    note right
      **Recovery State Transition (80% Hysteresis)**
      Robot.status: **CHARGING -> IDLE**
      (batteryPolicy.js: BATTERY_MODE.OK)
    end note

    |Backend|
    :Mark charging incident and maintenance ticket as resolved;
    note right
      **Entity State Transition**
      BM01 Intended: IncidentLog.status: **LOGGED -> RESOLVED**
      (DB Implementation: SupportRequest.status = **"Completed"**)
    end note
  endif

  |Backend|
repeat while (Active fleet monitoring session continues?) is (Yes - Next telemetry cycle) not (No - Monitoring session ended)

stop

@enduml

